    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let's denote the measure of the angle as \\( x \\) degrees. The complement of an angle is what, when added to the angle, equals 90 degrees. Therefore, the complement of \\( x \\) is \\( 90 - x \\) degrees.\n\nAccording to the problem, the measure of the angle is double the measure of its complement. This relationship can be expressed with the equation:\n\n\\[ x = 2(90 - x) \\]\n\nExpanding the right side of the equation gives us:\n\n\\[ x = 180 - 2x \\]\n\nTo solve for \\( x \\), we add \\( 2x \\) to both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[ x + 2x = 180 \\]\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n\\[ 3x = 180 \\]\n\nDividing both sides by 3, we find:\n\n\\[ x = \\frac{180}{3} = 60 \\]\n\nTherefore, the measure of the angle is \\( \\boxed{60} \\) degrees.",
